{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"ArcaniaBot","id":"810907841329627137","is_bot":1,"username":"ArcaniaBot"},"author_id":"810907841329627137","channel_id":"851856616469823528","content":"?shutdown [halt]\n\n***Maintenance-only command***\nSave all data and close the bot, and disable automatic restart.\nData persisted between bot runs:\n- people's last locations\n- most recent day on which each daily message was sent\n- nicknames of active server members\n\nBy default, the bot will be automatically restarted within 5 minutes (on the next full 5 minutes mark).\nTo disable that behaviour, pass to the `halt` parameter value: `and halt, yes, seriously`\nWith halt state enabled, the automatic uptime script __**WILL NOT FIRE**__.\nHalt state can only be switched off through manual access.","created_at":"2021-06-08T17:55:43.498000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"851882199212228619","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Versil","id":"148682928434577408","is_bot":0,"username":"versil"},"author_id":"148682928434577408","channel_id":"851856616469823528","content":"manual access = ssh to the server, or dropbox. it'll be a file `Dropbox/arcania/bot/savestates/_HALT_STATE`. remove it and the automatic restart will resume","created_at":"2021-06-08T17:57:18.450000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"851882597470044190","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
